			"notes": "for minecraft 1.21.1. requires geckolib, biolith, and lib39 (also attached here, not included for technical reasons)\n\nmajor changes:\n- updated to minecraft 1.21.1!!\n  - you will need to download lib39 separately from the release page, for Reasons\n  - replaced the terrablender dependency with biolith\n  - note: the warded/infested block indicators no longer have their fancy visual effect\n  - note: aspect power status effects don't have their full functionality\n\nadditions:\n- the Zombified Thaumaturge! a hostile mob that eases you into progression\n  - spawns in any biome where zombies do\n  - shoots orbs of fire to attack\n  - drops the Scribbled Notes (if you don't already have arcana progress) and some Thaumium Nuggets\n- the Crystal Caverns! an underground biome with crystal formations\n  - contains Balanced Crystal, (new) Crystal Embedded Rock, Norite, and Exposed Norite\n  - spawns Mites, weaker forms of Wisps\n    - these still require further progression to interact with, and can only drop Twisted Essence\n- the Holding Jug! an earlygame storage item\n  - does not have a maximum item capacity, instead storing a limited number of aspect types & a limited aspect total\n- the Diamond-Tipped Claw Ring, and it's upgraded form, the Ruby-Tipped Feral Claw Ring! early & lategame equippable weapons\n  - increases your unarmed damage, and fills your hunger on kills\n  - the ruby variant (currently unobtainable in survival) grants more damage, hunger, runic shielding, and refills your runic shielding on kills\n- the Mirrored Amulet! a midgame equippable\n  - acts like a Personal Magic Mirror, allowing you to send and receive items from your inventory\n  - when equipped, if you die, your items are sent through the mirror (rather than dropped on the ground)\n    - has no effect when `keepInventory` is on\n- spawn eggs for all arcana mobs\n- various decorative variants of Arcane Stone, including Pillars and Slates\n\nchanges:\n- the Lamplight Ring is now the Lamplight Amulet, is equipped in the necklace slot, and has an appropriately changed recipe\n  - rings generally have \"active\" effects, while amulets typically have purely passive effects, so this felt fitting\n  - also provides an earlygame amulet to wear, and keeps it out of competition with other stronger rings\n- renamed and rethemed some aspects\n  - Tempestas (Weather) -> Atmos (Atmosphere, Sky, Climate)\n  - Crystallo (Crystal) -> Crystallo (Crystal, Stability, Confinement)\n  - Motus (Movement) -> Kinesis (Movement, Force)\n- reorganised the creative inventory tab\n- improved the Mystic Mist's visuals\n- looking at a node will now show all aspects it generates, including ones it currently has 0 of\n- updated the Tainted Rock texture (thanks anatevka!)\n- improved dynamic lights support, Lux phials and crystals now glow\n- adjusted some research entry text\n- damage from Prismatic Light and Putrefaction now have custom sound effects, and the former now has a custom death message\n- improved Prismatic Light visuals\n- wand interaction recipes can now be done in the inventory, by holding a wand in the cursor and right-clicking on another item\n\nfixes:\n- fixed Adorned Ring not listing its discount in its tooltip\n- fixed nodes in structures (particularly the Crimson Camp) being duplicted when they spawn on a chunk boundary\n- fixed nodes in structures not spawning with full aspects\n- fixed missing tag and aspect assignments\n  - with new 1.21.1 items in particular, certain aspects (esp. Atmos and Iracundia) are now much more available\n- fixed Crystal Cluster blocks not being placeable on solid faces of non-solid blocks (e.g. stairs)\n- fixed attempting to cast a continuous wand focus (e.g. Fetch, Prismatic Light) with an empty wand causing visual issues\n- fixed overworld surface nodes being aligned to chunk boundaries\n\ntechnical changes (that are worth mentioning):\n- added biome tag `#arcana:zombie_thaumaturge_spawn_blacklist` for biomes where Zombie Thaumaturges cannot spawn\n\n..."
		},
